[size=5]Cartur's Farming[/size]

More to the Farming skill you already have, and a better way to plant whole fields. The better a farmer you are, the faster your crops grow and the more each one gives.

Inspired by [b]Smoothbrain's Farming[/b] (deprecated in 2026) and [b]Advize's PlantEasily[/b] - credit to both for the ideas. This is a separate mod, written from scratch for Valheim 1.0; it shares no code with either.

[size=4]The Farming skill[/size]

Everything builds on the game's own Farming skill, which you level by planting and harvesting. There is no second skill to grind.

[list]
[*][b]Any level[/b] - crops grow faster, twice as fast at 100. Speed comes from the level of whoever planted it.
[*][b]Any level[/b] - bigger harvests, double at 100, on top of the game's own bonus chance.
[*][b]Any level[/b] - planting costs 1% less stamina per level. Free at 100.
[*][b]Level 20[/b] - plant a whole field in one go, and harvest the same crop around you in one go - beehives too.
[*][b]Level 30[/b] - look at a planted crop to see how far grown it is.
[*][b]Level 50[/b] - crops you plant grow in any biome. Ashlands heat and northern cold still need a shield, as in the game.
[/list]

[size=4]Planting fields (level 20)[/size]

With the cultivator out, the crop you place is the corner of a field. Columns run to your right, rows away from you.

[list]
[*][b]Right Ctrl + arrow keys[/b] - more or fewer rows and columns, up to 10 x 10.
[*]Every cell shows a preview first: [b]red[/b] where a crop can't grow - no room, not hoed, a ward, or you've run out of seeds.
[*]Each crop is paid for: seeds, stamina and wards all apply, and it stops when you run out.
[*]Extra crops get a random turn so the field doesn't look stamped.
[*][b]F10[/b] - snap new crops onto the grid of the nearest crop, to extend a field.
[*][b]F6[/b] - replant crops as you harvest them, from the seeds in your bag.
[*][b]F8[/b] - turn field planting and group harvesting off and on.
[/list]

[size=4]Multiplayer[/size]

Install it on the server too and its Farming numbers apply to everyone. Keys and field settings stay your own.

[size=4]Compatibility[/size]

Don't run it alongside PlantEasily: both plant fields, and every crop would go in twice. If PlantEasily is installed this mod leaves fields, snapping, replanting and group harvest to it and keeps the skill side.

Source: [url=https://github.com/jekkle/cartur-farming]github.com/jekkle/cartur-farming[/url]

